-
-Source-only successor to the actual IHG R2 helper. The helper protocol and package are R3; the fixed input is `London`. `state`, `inspect`, `click`, and `set_text` pass the same operation entry sets in Java, the wire validator, and the adapter plan validator.
+# ihg owned helper R4 for current cell baseline02
 
-The original action method is byte-for-byte preserved: prior inspection scope/age/hash, full-tree/window equality, refreshed node hash and exact editable resource, final full tree/window, one ACTION_SET_TEXT, acknowledgement and exact value readback. Each adapter sequence retains its independent after-state in finally. The former public query is rejected. Prior helper UIDs 10196 and 10153 are excluded; the new installed UID is unknown.
+This create-only source/build candidate binds the actual baseline02 receipt, typed v2 host scope, and exact R6 host manifest. It derives from the fixed prior helper source manifest `8d96686f9e6937548e0295679ae6ecdfd3c3a1bf4e48c5feff7def949e81789a`.
 
-Static build runs the unchanged 21 current-baseline controls and 45 new direct production request/plan/selector/wire/UID controls, then the original 11-tool build plan. This source has not been compiled or run. Build roots are create-only source-01/build-01 in the R3 namespace. Static build performs no Android installation or UI operation.
+The commercial target package, UID, resource selectors, complete-tree/window/freshness checks, public input restrictions, action count limits, independent restoration, and time/resource bounds remain unchanged. Protocol and helper package are a new generation. The prior actual helper UID 10156 is rejected at the Session and wire result identity gates. Its historical receipt gives no runtime authority in this cell.
 
-A later current flow must first complete Search and Destination and then identify a unique eligible EditText and its bounded public Destination ancestor from a fresh complete owned tree. The historical resource hash and retired task 871 are diagnostic references. No prior node, path, token, nonce, task, installed UID or APK signer is granted new authority. Device input and business result qualification remain separate future steps.
+The build runs the original App-specific controls and 32 current-baseline/protocol/identity controls, then the pinned Java/APK toolchain. This source freeze has not executed Python or Java. APK, signer, and new installed UID remain unknown until separate actual build and install receipts. No business flow, old task, or issued nonce is reauthorized. Whole-App production readiness remains false.
